      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The critical side of the debate on meritocracy is rooted in the inherent flaws of IQ and standardized testing, which are inherently tied to systemic inequalities and privilege. For instance, research has shown that IQ scores are influenced by socioeconomic status, access to quality education, and cultural background, rendering them a poor predictor of individual merit. Furthermore, standardized testing often favors students from affluent, well-educated, and highly motivated backgrounds, perpetuating existing social hierarchies. This is evident in the disparate test scores of students from low-income and minority communities, who are often subjected to inadequate resources and biased curricula.",
